    <p>These are Standard-tier prices on the Gemini API [3]. Google prices Hydrogen flat across its full 1 million-token context window, and the pricing page lists no step-up date [1][2][3]. What’s new says the free tier is rate-limited, and that implicit caching gives cached input a 95% discount. Explicit caching is not supported [2][3]. The pricing page says free-tier content is used to improve Google’s products, and paid-tier content is not [3]. Every token the model processes is counted and billed, including thinking tokens and internal tool system instructions and function declarations when using grounding [2][3]. Batch and Flex are $0.75 input and $3.75 output, and are not available on the free tier. Priority is $2.70 input and $13.50 output. Contributor is an invite-only private preview at $0.75 input and $3.75 output; content on that tier is used to improve Google’s products [3].</p>
